ions that are not traditionally  Republican even though he he won as a  Republican president that kind of  cross-current appeal to the  working-class voters voters on all sides  that have felt ignored by the elites in  the Republican establishment the  Democratic establishment they felt for a  long time that their wages were not  increasing they couldn't get decent jobs  they were in the industrial Rust Belt  particularly in the Midwest states like  Pennsylvania and Donald Trump gave them  a voice he spoke to them and you know  what because he's post ideological he  has solutions-oriented  he is not ideologically based he is  Lucian's oriented so if you're a  Democrat and if you if your candidate  pulls us out in this district the lesson  is to reject the far-left approach that  was begun by Obama and perpetuated by  Nancy Pelosi and the other radicals that  are controlling the Democratic Party  their eyes should be open tonight and  they should see even if they lose this  is very close race they should see that  the path to electoral success does not  go through far-left radicalism governor  Rendell got about 15 seconds let's say  Ciccone had run as an establishment  Republican not in favor of tariffs where  do you think this race would have been  tonight again we don't know where it's  going to turn out but don't you think  Connor Lam would have been I had like 10  points at least well at least three or  four no question and look tariffs I  testified about imposing a tariff when I  was governor because China was dumping  steel into the into the u.s. to try to  drive out our steel industry the thing  that Donald Trump did wrong Laura is he  did it to broad-based you should do it  against transgressors people who were  dumping he got a lot of leverage against  the EU and we're gonna see where that  leverage lead

